0,Autonomous Region of Bougainville - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonomous_Region_of_Bougainville,"Bougainville, officially the Autonomous Region of Bougainville, is an autonomous region in Papua New Guinea. The largest island is Bougainville Island, while the region also includes Buka Island and a number of outlying islands and atolls.",Askopan,North Bougainville
1,Askopan Language (EIV) – L1 & L2 Speakers... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/eiv/,"Askopan is a stable indigenous language of Papua New Guinea. It belongs to the North Bougainville language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.",Askopan,North Bougainville
2,Askopan language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/askopan_language,"The Askopan language, also known as Eivo, is a Papuan language spoken primarily in Central Bougainville, an island in Papua New Guinea, by approximately 1,200 people. It belongs to the North Bougainvi.",Askopan,North Bougainville
3,Bougainville languages - Sorosoro Sorosoro,https://www.sorosoro.org/en/bougainville-languages/,"North Bougainville. Ramopa. Rapoisi. Askopan. Rotokas. Comments on the classification of Bougainville languages: These two branches have sometimes been classified separately, their grouping together is perhaps more geographic than linguistic.",Askopan,North Bougainville
